# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in what you have. Nothing here reaches
# the repository; `synpath doctor` reports what loads.

# Kalshi: API key id and its private key file (PEM, Ed25519 or RSA, the BEGIN...END
# block only), from kalshi.com/account/profile -> API Keys. REST market data needs
# neither; the WebSocket (books) and trading need both.
KALSHI_KEY_ID=
KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/Users/you/.kalshi/kalshi.pem
# prod (the default) trades real money on Kalshi; demo uses Kalshi's practice exchange with a demo key.
KALSHI_ENV=prod

# Polymarket (global CLOB V2). The signer's private key, hex, and the wallet the
# orders spend from: signature type 3 with the Deposit Wallet address as funder
# for any account created since May 2026 (polymarket.com -> profile menu);
# 1 or 2 for legacy proxy / Safe wallets; 0 only for an allowlisted EOA.
POLYMARKET_PRIVATE_KEY=
POLYMARKET_SIGNATURE_TYPE=3
POLYMARKET_FUNDER=
# Optional: existing CLOB API credentials (derived from the key when absent),
# a builder code, a Relayer API key for gasless approvals / split / merge /
# redeem, and a Polygon RPC endpoint for an EOA's own transactions.
POLYMARKET_API_KEY=
POLYMARKET_API_SECRET=
POLYMARKET_API_PASSPHRASE=
POLYMARKET_BUILDER_CODE=
POLYMARKET_RELAYER_API_KEY=
POLYMARKET_RELAYER_API_KEY_ADDRESS=
POLYMARKET_RPC_URL=

# Polymarket US, retail API (api.polymarket.us): key id and base64 secret from
# polymarket.us/developer after identity verification in the app.
POLYMARKET_US_KEY_ID=
POLYMARKET_US_SECRET_KEY=

# Polymarket US, exchange API (polymarketexchange.com): an onboarded firm's
# client id, RSA private key file, participant id and trading account.
POLYMARKET_US_CLIENT_ID=
POLYMARKET_US_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
POLYMARKET_US_PARTICIPANT_ID=
POLYMARKET_US_ACCOUNT=
POLYMARKET_US_ENV=preprod

# Opinion (opinion.trade, BNB Chain): the Open API key alone serves market data
# and the WebSocket (synpath init creates one by signing with your wallet). To
# trade, also the private key (64 hex, not the 0x address) of the wallet
# connected on opinion.trade. The account's Safe is read from the venue if unset.
OPINION_API_KEY=
OPINION_PRIVATE_KEY=
OPINION_MULTISIG_ADDRESS=

# Hyperliquid (outcome markets, HIP-4): an API wallet's key is safest -- it
# trades but cannot withdraw (app.hyperliquid.xyz -> More -> API). With an API
# wallet, set the account it trades for. HYPERLIQUID_TESTNET=1 uses the test
# network. Market data and streams need none of this.
HYPERLIQUID_PRIVATE_KEY=
HYPERLIQUID_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
HYPERLIQUID_TESTNET=

# predict.fun (BNB Chain): every mainnet request needs an API key, market data
# included, and that key is all market data needs (pred_sk_..., from
# https://developers.predict.fun). To trade, also the private key
# that signs: a plain wallet's own, or, for a Predict account (made by the web
# app), its owner key (Account -> Settings -> Privy wallet) with the account's
# deposit address. PREDICT_FUN_TESTNET=1 uses the test network, which needs no
# API key. PREDICT_FUN_RPC_URL (optional) is the node the balance is read from.
PREDICT_FUN_API_KEY=
PREDICT_FUN_PRIVATE_KEY=
PREDICT_FUN_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
PREDICT_FUN_TESTNET=
PREDICT_FUN_RPC_URL=

# Limitless (Base): market data needs nothing. To trade, the private key of the
# wallet connected on limitless.exchange (in EOA trading mode) and a scoped API
# token derived there (profile, API tokens, Derive): its id and base64 secret.
# LIMITLESS_RPC_URL (optional) is the Base node the balance is read from.
LIMITLESS_PRIVATE_KEY=
LIMITLESS_API_TOKEN_ID=
LIMITLESS_API_SECRET=
LIMITLESS_RPC_URL=

# SX Bet: REST market data needs nothing. SX_BET_API_KEY (sx.bet -> Account ->
# Overview -> API Credentials) serves the live streams, reads the account's
# orders, fills, positions and balance, and cancels. SX_BET_PRIVATE_KEY is
# needed only to place orders: the key of the wallet you sign in to sx.bet with
# (the account's own, not its proxy wallet). Without it, SX_BET_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS
# (the wallet's public 0x address, not its private key) lets the account stream
# run; unset, the account is polled. SX_BET_TESTNET=1 uses the Toronto test
# network, whose key is made on toronto.sx.bet.
SX_BET_API_KEY=
SX_BET_PRIVATE_KEY=
SX_BET_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
SX_BET_TESTNET=

# Betfair Exchange (market data and streams; no order entry yet): every call,
# market data included, needs your own account and application key. The free
# delayed key (1-180 s late, three price levels) is on the developer program
# page or the Accounts API visualiser. Leave the certificate paths empty for an
# interactive login; set both for Betfair's certificate login. The site the
# account is on: com (default), it, es, ro or com.au. Betfair's API is refused
# from the US and several other countries, and showing its prices to others
# needs a Betfair data licence.
BETFAIR_APP_KEY=
BETFAIR_USERNAME=
BETFAIR_PASSWORD=
BETFAIR_CERT_PATH=
BETFAIR_KEY_PATH=
BETFAIR_JURISDICTION=

# Smarkets (market data and a polled stream; no order entry yet): market data
# needs no login at all. A login (optional) sends a session token for
# undelayed quotes and your account's own rate limits. Betting through the API
# needs Smarkets' approved API access (a one-off £150 fee). Smarkets' API terms
# allow viewing prices and betting on your own account; odds scraping is
# prohibited.
SMARKETS_USERNAME=
SMARKETS_PASSWORD=

# Novig: market data needs nothing. To trade, a subaccount's trading key: its
# key id and its private key file (PKCS#8 PEM, Ed25519 or P-256). Make the
# management key in the web app (Profile -> Settings -> Novig API), then open a
# subaccount with it (NovigTrading.open_subaccount), which issues the trading
# key. The management key (optional here) opens, funds and labels subaccounts
# and never places an order. NOVIG_ENV is production (real money, US identity
# and location checks; Arizona, Michigan and Nevada are restricted) or paper
# (play money at paper.novig.com). A key works only in the environment it was
# made in.
NOVIG_KEY_ID=
NOVIG_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
NOVIG_ENV=
NOVIG_MANAGEMENT_KEY_ID=
NOVIG_MANAGEMENT_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=

# Matchbook (market data, a polled stream, and order entry): market data needs
# no login at all. Betting logs in with your Matchbook username and password;
# an account with two-factor login cannot log in from here. Every GET is
# chargeable on Matchbook's API plans (£100 per million a month), and its terms
# allow viewing prices and betting on your own account only.
MATCHBOOK_USERNAME=
MATCHBOOK_PASSWORD=

# ProphetX: every call, market data included, needs a key. The Trading API key
# pair (any KYC-approved account: prophetx.co -> Menu -> API Integration; the
# secret is shown once) reads market data, streams it and places orders; run
# each process on its own pair, since ProphetX counts sessions per key.
# PROPHETX_AFFILIATE_KEY (optional) is a Market Data API key that ProphetX's
# market data team issues on request; it reads market data only.
# PROPHETX_SANDBOX=1 uses ProphetX's sandbox, whose keys are made on
# sandbox.prophetx.dev.
PROPHETX_ACCESS_KEY=
PROPHETX_SECRET_KEY=
PROPHETX_AFFILIATE_KEY=
PROPHETX_SANDBOX=

# Azuro (onchain sports betting pool): market data needs nothing. To bet, the
# private key of the wallet that signs each bet and holds the bet token (USDT on
# Polygon, WETH on Base); the wallet must also approve Azuro's relayer to spend
# the token once (AzuroTrading.approve(), an on-chain transaction). AZURO_CHAIN
# picks the pool: polygon (default), base, or the testnets polygon_amoy and
# base_sepolia. AZURO_AFFILIATE (optional) is the affiliate address each bet
# names, the wallet's own when unset. AZURO_RPC_URL (optional) is the node the
# balance and allowance are read from and the approval is sent through. Azuro's
# bet API and streams are refused from some regions.
AZURO_PRIVATE_KEY=
AZURO_CHAIN=
AZURO_AFFILIATE=
AZURO_RPC_URL=

# Myriad: market data needs nothing. MYRIAD_PRIVATE_KEY is the wallet your
# Myriad account is connected to: it signs every order and cancel. An API key
# and its secret (Myriad Account settings; the secret is shown once) sign the
# account's requests and raise the rate limit; the venue refuses a key without
# its secret. Without a key the wallet signs in for a session instead, and a
# wallet's first sign-in creates its Myriad account. A key alone reads the
# account: set MYRIAD_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS (the wallet's public 0x address, not its
# private key). MYRIAD_RPC_URL (optional) is the BNB Chain node the balance is
# read from.
MYRIAD_PRIVATE_KEY=
MYRIAD_API_KEY=
MYRIAD_API_SECRET=
MYRIAD_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
MYRIAD_RPC_URL=
